WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.148
This gate is an evidence checklist.

00:00:02.148 --> 00:00:03.938
Vibes do not unlock Systems.

00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:06.086
This lesson is about first-customer gate.

00:00:06.086 --> 00:00:08.591
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:08.591 --> 00:00:12.171
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:12.171 --> 00:00:17.541
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:17.541 --> 00:00:21.478
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:21.478 --> 00:00:25.416
Stay practical: complete evidence checklist before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:25.736 --> 00:00:30.663
Check: conversations logged, offers sent, money asked, payment path ready, onboarding draft.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.126
Remember the objective: complete evidence checklist.

00:00:33.126 --> 00:00:37.642
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:37.642 --> 00:00:42.569
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:42.569 --> 00:00:47.085
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:52.012
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:52.012 --> 00:00:54.886
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:54.886 --> 00:00:56.528
Feedback beats guessing alone.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:58.773
Complete the checklist to pass.

00:00:58.773 --> 00:01:01.852
Missing proof means more outreach, not more branding.

